---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---
<SiteLayout active="research" title="Research · Hyeongmuk Lim" description="Research interests in quantum geometry, band topology, and theoretical condensed matter physics.">
  <section class="container page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">RESEARCH</p>
    <h1>Geometry meets <em>quantum matter.</em></h1>
    <p class="intro-lead">My research explores the information encoded in quantum wave functions beyond energy spectra, and its consequences for topological and correlated phases.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container research-details">
    <article id="quantum-geometry" class="research-detail">
      <div class="detail-num">01 / Quantum geometry</div>
      <div><h2>Geometry of quantum states</h2><p>Quantum geometry describes how wave functions evolve across parameter or momentum space. I am interested in the quantum metric, Berry and non-Abelian curvature, and geometries that arise in multiband systems and Kramers pairs.</p><a href="/publications/#lim2026quaternion" class="text-arrow">Related publication →</a></div>
      <div class="detail-symbol">𝒬<sub>μν</sub></div>
    </article>
    <article id="band-topology" class="research-detail">
      <div class="detail-num">02 / Band topology</div>
      <div><h2>Beyond conventional band topology</h2><p>Some topological structures depend on more information than occupied-band topology or the low-energy nodal spectrum alone. Hopf and real Hopf invariants, delicate topology, and unconventional transitions are representative examples.</p><a href="/publications/#lim2023hopf" class="text-arrow">Related publication →</a></div>
      <div class="detail-symbol">π<sub>3</sub></div>
    </article>
    <article id="many-body" class="research-detail">
      <div class="detail-num">03 / Quantum many-body</div>
      <div><h2>Geometry and correlations</h2><p>A longer-term direction is to understand how nontrivial quantum geometry and symmetry can organize interacting many-body phenomena, particularly in narrow-band systems.</p><a href="/notes/" class="text-arrow">Notes & learning →</a></div>
      <div class="detail-symbol">⟨ψ⟩</div>
    </article>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
